{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/769599-s~q_rpg_itlot","id":769599,"title":"S~Q_RPG_ITLOT","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T15:40:04-08:00","id":769599,"title":"S~Q_RPG_ITLOT","content":"Did the Heavy acronyms get your attention? Well then good that shows that your smarter than most, LOL. (Used acronyms for IP Security.) I am first of all looking for people who want to polish my game up some. I don't mind paying for a job well done. If you want to play, we can discuss that too. There are many ways to do so, I think LOL. My game runs fairly simple, and you can even keep a simplified version of your character sheet in your wallet. (The size of a business card.)<br /> <br /> Workers Wanted:<br /> <br /> Artist:<br /> Landscapers, Architects, Naturalist. (Landscapes, flora/fauna, structures)<br /> Artist who know how to follow instruction. Some art needs to be exact, since my world isn't like any I have seen, yet. The rest, doesn't matter too much. I don't mind paying regularly for good art. If you got the talent, I will put you on my pay roll, lol.<br /> <br /> <br /> Coders:<br /> Someone who can make a few applications, like interactive character sheets, or other tools that will help me facilitate good gaming. Or even direct me to places that ALREADY have tools.<br /> <br /> About the Game:<br /> <br /> If you like realistic gaming with actual scientific principles, then this game will also work for you. For example; your character wants to make a flame thrower, (as I already had a player do, and it was marvelous.) then look up how to build one, find the materials in the game, make it and you can build it. I don't limit your knowledge, I rather want to cultivate it.<br /> <br /> If you want to IMPORT a character, then I already have a test that your character can run through that's part of the game with out being in 'my world' as it were. If it survives, then so be it. Native's need not to go through the trial. Nor do they get anything earned from that experience. They do have bonus's that deal with being native.<br /> <br /> I don't play favorites, not even with my own characters. So don't even go there. I do reward various virtues, as well as wisdom and intelligence, when I personally see that it is good and helps the party/story/world/rules etc. Understand, this is 'my world' that is based in the actual reality I understand and live in. There are certain things that apply to certain races/professions, that may not apply to others. Some choices have HARD consequences, safety first and all that. LOL<br /> <br /> Bonus's/Prizes*:<br /> <br /> Yes I offer character bonus's often on several factors. And yes I will offer actual prizes occasionally, for players who have been good consistent players, based on story, achievements etc.<br /> <br /> Setting:<br /> <br /> In my game I have an OPTION that a character with the most of a certain stat, determines what setting it is in. Yes my game runs on various timelines, and yes you can alter the timeline and change the world, possibly. The players I mentioned earlier, sure did. It was a nice addition. I just hope it didn't make it too easy to pass the test now, in that specific timeline.<br /> Generally, it is like dnd. However not limited to that era alone.<br /> <br /> World Size:<br /> <br /> According to that smart fellow who built the flame thrower, who was smart enough to calculate general size, said it was the size of Jupiter. I didn't think I have that much running around in my head. I checked his math, it is WAY big, just not THAT BIG. Maybe Neptune, or some other big planet. (*Automatic skill profession: 'Astronomer' to the first player who can give the most accurate comparison. I might add an in game item also. Or might even send a trinket, if I can find one appropriate.)<br /> <br /> Class/Race/Job/Profession:<br /> <br /> Outlanders can be of anything, because they are outlanders, having to earn their way in. Good luck with that! Its not all that hard, its just not nerfed/watered down/ sugar coated/ dumbed down.<br /> <br /> Native Born:<br /> Typical RPG Races as well as a few sub species and unique ones. There is a 'catch' you have to wait for it to find out LOL. We will talk about character creation on a personal level, because its personal, and your character. It is sacred, unless you want to play canned meat/meat shield/beat stick. LOL<br /> <br /> Professions: If you can make a living at it, then it can be your class. Yes through wisdom and knowledge even a fisherman or a cook can be a deadly BAD @$$ character. Allot of players already found that out. None of my personal characters aren't that fancy however. Questions? We can go over that in time.<br /> <br /> If you want to play its going to be AWESOME, especially if your local.....no....no don't ask it....NO I DONT LARP LOL.<br /> <br /> Recruitment:<br /> <br /> If you want to help spread this around like butter on toast, then get to it. Just remember it is my game, and be respectful. Yes there can be character rewards for helping out this way also.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?770925-S-Q_RPG_ITLOT&amp;p=19589630#post19589630\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...0#post19589630</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9511,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9511-sirlol","user":"SirLOL","date":".  added link 11-25-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9511-sirlol","name":"SirLOL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9511_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}